Project name: XPLOR

XPLOR is a full-stack web project with a futuristic AI-startup style. The frontend is no longer just placeholder scaffolding: the landing page now has a clear visual direction, multiple sections, and animated styling. The backend is still minimal and ready to be expanded into a real authentication/API system.

Tech stack:
- Frontend: React + Vite
- Routing: React Router
- Backend: Node.js + Express
- Planned database: MongoDB + Mongoose
- Planned auth: bcryptjs + JWT

Frontend libraries already installed:
- `framer-motion`
- `gsap`
- `three`
- `@react-three/fiber`
- `@react-three/drei`
- `axios`
- `react-icons`
- `lucide-react`

Backend libraries already installed:
- `express`
- `cors`
- `dotenv`
- `mongoose`
- `bcryptjs`
- `jsonwebtoken`

Project structure:
- `client/` -> React frontend
- `server/` -> Express backend

Current frontend routing:
- `/` -> Home
- `/login` -> Login
- `/signup` -> Signup
- `/dashboard` -> Dashboard

Current app entry:
- `client/src/main.jsx` mounts the app inside `BrowserRouter`
- `client/src/App.jsx` defines the route structure

What the project currently is:
This is an AI/startup-style SaaS landing page plus the beginning of an auth-based product. The public homepage is being designed first, while login, signup, dashboard, API logic, and database logic still need to be built.

Current homepage structure:
`client/src/pages/Home.jsx` renders:
- `Navbar`
- `Hero`
- `Features`
- `Stats`
- `Footer`

Current homepage direction:
The visual style is futuristic, glowing, immersive, glassmorphism-based, gradient-heavy, and motion-friendly. The design language is dark, neon, animated, and startup-marketing focused.

Current components and intent:

1. `Navbar.jsx`
- Fixed top navbar
- Brand name: `XPLOR`
- Nav links: Home, About, Features, Contact
- CTA buttons: Login and Sign Up
- Login links to `/login`
- Sign Up links to `/signup`

2. `Hero.jsx`
- Main landing hero section
- Messaging:
  - "AI Powered Startup Platform"
  - "Explore The Future With XPLOR"
- Includes:
  - gradient animated headline
  - descriptive paragraph
  - primary and secondary CTA buttons
  - decorative glowing circles
  - floating orb
  - glassmorphism hero card
- Current hero theme suggests:
  - AI automation
  - futuristic dashboards
  - immersive startup tools
  - strong visual motion

3. `Features.jsx`
- Section heading: why choose XPLOR
- 6 feature cards:
  - AI Automation
  - Analytics Dashboard
  - 3D Experience
  - Cloud Security
  - Team Collaboration
  - Smart Insights
- This establishes the product as an AI business/startup platform rather than a generic website

4. `Stats.jsx`
- Marketing stats section with 4 cards:
  - 10K+ Users Worldwide
  - 95% Customer Satisfaction
  - 24/7 AI Support
  - 500+ Companies Using XPLOR

5. `Footer.jsx`
- Brand summary
- Quick links
- Contact info
- Social icons
- Positioning remains brand/marketing focused

Current styling direction:
Global and section CSS already define the current art direction. The existing style is not neutral or plain. Any future AI should preserve and extend this direction rather than replacing it with a generic template.

Current visual traits:
- dark futuristic background
- neon purple / blue / cyan gradients
- blur and glow effects
- glassmorphism cards
- fixed translucent navbar
- animated gradient backgrounds
- floating shapes/orbs
- hover lift effects
- premium startup landing page tone

Animation already present in CSS:
- animated moving hero background gradients
- animated glowing background blobs
- animated gradient text
- animated gradient buttons
- floating orb motion
- floating card motion
- glowing pulse/scale effects on circles

Important design instruction for future AI:
Do not downgrade this into a plain business site.
Do not replace the current futuristic aesthetic with basic cards, default layouts, or flat white sections.
Build further in the same high-energy visual direction:
- premium
- immersive
- animated
- modern SaaS / AI startup
- polished and cinematic where appropriate

What is still incomplete on the frontend:
- `Login.jsx` is still a placeholder
- `Signup.jsx` is still a placeholder
- `Dashboard.jsx` is still a placeholder
- `auth.css` is empty
- There is no real authentication state yet
- There is no protected route logic yet
- CTA buttons on the homepage do not yet drive full product flows
- Navbar links like About, Features, Contact do not appear to scroll to real anchored sections yet
- Mobile responsiveness is not fully implemented in the current CSS
- Advanced JS-based animations are not implemented yet, even though animation libraries are installed

Important implementation notes:
- There is a filename case inconsistency:
  - `Features.jsx` imports `../styles/features.css`
  - actual file is `client/src/styles/Features.css`
- There is another filename case inconsistency:
  - `Stats.jsx` imports `../styles/stats.css`
  - actual file is `client/src/styles/Stats.css`
- This may still work on Windows but can break on case-sensitive systems. Any AI modifying the project should fix or preserve this carefully.
- Footer copyright text currently contains an encoding issue:
  - `Â© 2026 XPLOR. All Rights Reserved.`

Current backend status:
`server/server.js` currently:
- loads environment variables with `dotenv`
- enables `cors`
- enables JSON body parsing
- exposes only one route:
  - `GET /` -> `XPLOR API Running`
- listens on `PORT` or `5000`

What is not built yet on the backend:
- no MongoDB connection logic
- no models
- no auth controllers
- no auth routes
- no JWT middleware
- no protected endpoints
- no user persistence
- no dashboard API data

Product intention inferred from current code:
XPLOR is intended to become an AI-powered startup/business platform with:
- a strong public landing page
- signup/login flow
- a user dashboard
- analytics and AI/business-oriented product messaging
- possibly immersive or 3D-enhanced UI later, since `three` and React Three Fiber are installed

Safe assumptions for future AI:
- The homepage should continue becoming more polished and animated
- Auth pages should match the same futuristic/glassmorphism style
- Dashboard should feel premium and data-rich, not plain
- Motion and interactions should be enhanced using existing libraries where useful
- The next AI can extend with:
  - scroll reveal animations
  - section transitions
  - animated counters
  - parallax/glow interactions
  - better CTA behavior
  - responsive layouts
  - auth UI and API integration

What future AI should NOT assume:
- The backend auth system already exists
- The dashboard has real data
- The frontend is connected to the backend
- The app has protected routes
- The current landing page is fully production-ready
- The nav links are fully functional
- The design system is fully finished

Recommended next build order:
1. polish and make homepage fully responsive
2. add richer animations using Framer Motion or GSAP
3. build styled Login and Signup pages that match the homepage
4. create backend auth routes and user model
5. connect frontend auth forms to backend with Axios
6. add JWT-based protected routing
7. build a real dashboard UI
8. later add premium extras like 3D/interactive visual elements if needed

Summary:
XPLOR is an early-stage full-stack AI-startup web app. The public landing page now has a real futuristic brand direction with glowing gradients, glassmorphism, and built-in CSS animations. The project should be continued in that same premium animated style. Authentication, backend logic, database models, protected routing, and dashboard functionality are still mostly unbuilt and should be developed next without losing the current visual identity.
